        },
        "2916552a-4524-4aff-acbc-634e4afb6d00": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "parent_column": "right",
            "reveal": true,
            "title": "Cairo",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>With millennia-old history and boasting some of the world's most extraordinary ancient wonders, including the Great Pyramid of Giza and the Great Sphinx, Cairo is the bustling capital of Egypt. It showcases its timeless charm and significance as a cultural, historical, and political hub.</p>",
            "dropdown_image": "shopify://shop_images/egypt-tour-day-cairo.jpg",
            "background_color": "#2e2767",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "aaa35b1a-8f7f-40b4-88b2-307c26dd6c43": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "parent_column": "right",
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Luxor",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>Luxor is iconic for its unparalleled wealth of ancient Egyptian temples and monuments, making it a living museum of ancient history and civilization. Known as the \"world's greatest open-air museum,\" Luxor's historical richness and grandeur continue to awe and inspire visitors from around the world.</p>",
            "dropdown_image": "shopify://shop_images/luxor-1200x800.jpg",
            "background_color": "#2e2767",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "643bace9-4996-4be4-b931-2de728a157a3": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "parent_column": "right",
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Valley of the Kings",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>Known for its status as the final resting place of numerous ancient Egyptian pharaohs, including the famous Tutankhamun, this ancient necropolis holds great historical significance. The discovery of stunning tombs filled with treasures continues to captivate the world's imagination.</p>",
            "dropdown_image": "shopify://shop_images/Valley_of_the_Kings.jpg",
            "background_color": "#2e2767",
            "text_color": "#f4f5f7"
          }
        },
        "cab40b70-71f5-4157-900c-344ccf2d5e06": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "parent_column": "right",
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Giza Plateau",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>The Giza Plateau is marked by a number of extraordinary megaliths in addition to the pyramids, most notably the Great Sphinx. It also contains important clues to an alternative history as researchers have identified the unmistakable signs of water erosion on the side of the bedrock in which the Sphinx was carved, hinting at its pre-diluvian origin.</p>",
            "dropdown_image": "shopify://shop_images/Giza_Plateau_2.jpg",
            "background_color": "#2e2767",
            "text_color": "#f4f5f7"
          }
        },
        "bd48c292-e8fb-405b-9fc2-3e92ec363226": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "parent_column": "right",
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "The Great Pyramid",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>Precisely aligned within a fraction of a degree to Earth’s cardinal directions, the Great Pyramid is an unprecedented architectural marvel. While its origin has been attributed to the Egyptian Old Kingdom Pharaoh Khufu (aka Cheops), no remains were ever found, shrouding the original construction of this colossal monument in further mystery.</p>",
            "dropdown_image": "shopify://shop_images/Great_Pyramid_2.jpg",
            "background_color": "#2e2767",
            "text_color": "#f4f5f7"
          }
        }
      },
